'''''Streblus''''' is a genus of [[flowering plant]]s in the [[Morus (plant)|mulberry]] family, [[Moraceae]]. It includes five species native to the [[Indian subcontinent]], [[Indochina]], southern China, and Malesia.<ref name = powo/> 

==Species==
Five species are currently accepted.<ref name = powo/>
*''[[Streblus asper]]'' <small>[[João de Loureiro|Lour.]]</small> – Siamese rough bush
*''[[Streblus celebensis]]'' {{small|[[C.C.Berg]]}}
*''[[Streblus mitis]]'' {{small|Kurz}}
*''[[Streblus vidalii]]'' {{small|T.H.Nguyên}}
*''[[Streblus monoicus]]'' {{small|[[Gagnep.]]}}

===Formerly placed here===
*''[[Paratrophis banksii]]'' {{small|Cheeseman}} – large-leaved milk tree (as ''Streblus banksii'' {{small|(Cheeseman) C.J.Webb}})
*''[[Paratrophis microphylla]]'' {{small|(Raoul) Cockayne}} – small-leaved milk tree (as ''Streblus heterophyllus'' {{small|(Blume) Corner}})
* ''[[Paratrophis pendulina]]'' {{small|(Endl.) E.M.Gardner}} – ''a{{okina}}ia{{okina}}i'' (Eastern [[Australia]], [[Melanesia]], [[Micronesia]], [[Polynesia]])<ref name="CFTH">{{cite journal |url=http://www.ctahr.hawaii.edu/forestry/data/CommonTreesHI/CFT_Streblus_pendulinus.pdf |title=Aʻiaʻi, Hawaiian false-mulberry |first=Elbert L. |last=Little Jr. |author2=Roger G. Skolmen  |publisher=[[United States Forest Service]] |year=1989}}</ref> (as ''Streblus pendulinus'' <small>([[Stephan Endlicher|Endl.]]) [[Ferdinand von Mueller|F.Muell]]</small> and ''[[Streblus brunonianus]]'' {{small|(Endl.) F.Muell.}})
*''[[Paratrophis sclerophylla]]'' {{small|(Corner) E.M.Gardner}} (as ''Streblus sclerophyllus'' <small>[[E. J. H. Corner|Corner]]</small>)
*''[[Paratrophis smithii]]'' {{small|Cheeseman}} – Three Kings milk tree (as ''Streblus smithii'' {{small|(Cheeseman) Corner}})
*''[[Sloetia elongata]]'' {{small|(Miq.) Koord.}} (as ''Streblus elongatus'' {{small|(Miq.) Corner}})
*''[[Taxotrophis ilicifolia]]'' {{small|(Kurz) S.Vidal}} (as ''Streblus ilicifolius'' <small>(Vidal) Corner</small>)
*''[[Taxotrophis taxoides]]'' {{small|(B.Heyne ex Roth) Chew ex E.M.Gardner}} (as ''Streblus taxoides'' <small>(Roth) Kurz.</small>)

